{"id": "EUVD-2017-19019", "enisaUuid": "60f07ec6-9eac-3dd7-8afe-108d459fb066", "description": "DevIL through 1.8.0 contains a heap-based buffer overflow in iGetPalette() in il_gif.cpp that allows attackers to write beyond a 768-byte palette buffer when loading GIF images. Attackers can supply a crafted two-frame GIF whose second frame uses disposal method 1 with a local colour table, writing up to 384 controlled bytes past the heap allocation and possibly executing code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:55:35", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/DentonW/DevIL/issues/67", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/devil-gif-palette-reuse-heap-overflow", "https://github.com/DentonW/DevIL/blob/a2d9193fed0c7f93519c0c4c28b3348e0cb5759b/DevIL/src-IL/src/il_gif.cpp#L189-L226", "https://github.com/DentonW/DevIL/blob/a2d9193fed0c7f93519c0c4c28b3348e0cb5759b/DevIL/src-IL/src/il_gif.cpp#L314-L324", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/devil-through-1.8.0-heap-buffer-overflow-via-gif-igetpalette"], "aliases": ["CVE-2017-20286", "GHSA-5rw7-933r-f38v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5e8e800e-a3e6-330f-93d3-07311f50e8e7", "product": {"name": "DevIL", "vendor": {"name": "DentonW"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.8.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "808467c7-c7ca-320a-970d-d3fdcc3af76e", "vendor": {"name": "DentonW"}}], "isExploited": false}